---
import { Card } from "@origami-systems/ui";
import MainLayout from "~/layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout
    title="Terms of Use - Origami Systems"
    description="The terms for using Origami Systems apps and services."
>
    <article class="blog">
        <header>
            <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
            <div class="description">
                Effective date: November 19, 2026 · Last updated: November 19,
                2026
            </div>
        </header>
        <hr />
        <Card class="summary-card">
            <div class="summary">
                <h2>The short version</h2>
                <p class="summary-note">
                    This summary is here to help you understand the terms
                    quickly. It does not replace the full Terms of Use below.
                    The summary and the full terms are not separate agreements.
                    When you accept, you are accepting the full terms, and if
                    anything in this summary differs from the full text, the
                    full text controls.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        You must be 13 or older to create a personal account. If
                        you are under 18, a parent or guardian agrees for you.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        If you use the Services for an organization, you agree
                        on its behalf. Organization administrators control the
                        accounts they manage.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Your content stays yours. We use it only to run, secure,
                        and improve the Services.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Don't harass people, send spam, break in, scrape, or try
                        to see another organization's data.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        If you create a sign-up form, you are responsible for
                        what it asks and for choosing who can see the names of
                        people who sign up.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Paid plans renew until you cancel. Fees are not
                        refundable unless the law requires a refund.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        The Services come "as is," and our liability is limited.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        We can suspend accounts that break these terms. An
                        organization that closes gets 30 days to export its
                        data.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Texas law applies. If there is a dispute, contact us
                        first and we will try to work it out for 30 days before
                        anyone goes to court.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </Card>
        <div class="content">
            <p>
                These Terms of Use are an agreement between you and Origami
                Systems LLC ("Origami Systems," "we," "us," or "our"). They
                cover The House App, The Signups App, Origami Systems Identity,
                the Account app, our websites, and any other Origami Systems
                service that links to these terms (together, the "Services").
            </p>
            <p>
                You accept these terms when you check the box to accept them
                while creating a personal account, or when you otherwise use the
                Services. If you do not agree, do not use the Services.
            </p>
            <p>
                If you use the Services for a school, church, business, or other
                organization, you confirm that you have authority to accept
                these terms for it. In these terms, "Organization" means that
                organization, and "you" includes both you and the Organization
                where it applies.
            </p>
            <h2 id="the-services">The Services</h2>
            <p>
                The House App helps organizations run house systems, including
                members, points, games, events, announcements, comments, guests,
                and participation records.
            </p>
            <p>
                The Signups App lets people create sign-up forms, collect
                registrations, and manage slots, participants, and waitlists.
            </p>
            <p>
                Origami Systems Identity and the Account app provide sign-in and
                account management for the other Services.
            </p>
            <p>
                We may add, change, or remove features. If a change
                substantially reduces the features of a paid plan, we will give
                reasonable notice in advance.
            </p>
            <h2 id="eligibility-and-minors">Eligibility and minors</h2>
            <p>
                You must be at least 13 years old to create a personal account.
                If you are under 18, or under the age of majority where you
                live, a parent or guardian must agree to these terms for you.
            </p>
            <p>
                A child under 13 may use the Services only through an account
                provided by a school or other Organization that has obtained any
                consent the law requires.
            </p>
            <p>
                An Organization decides who may use its account and is
                responsible for giving its users any notices and getting any
                permissions or consents the law requires. This does not shift to
                the Organization any legal duty the law places directly on
                Origami Systems.
            </p>
            <h2 id="accounts">Accounts</h2>
            <h3>Personal accounts</h3>
            <p>
                You are responsible for the information in your personal account
                and for activity that happens through it. One personal account
                works across the Services that support it.
            </p>
            <p>
                You can delete your personal account in the Account app. We
                disable the account right away and delete it permanently 7 days
                later. You can cancel during those 7 days by signing in to the
                Account app. If you are the only administrator of an
                Organization, you must add another administrator before you can
                delete your account. Our Privacy Policy describes what happens
                to your data.
            </p>
            <h3>Organization-managed and guest accounts</h3>
            <p>
                An Organization may create accounts for its members or invite
                guests. The Organization controls those accounts, including
                their roles, access, and removal.
            </p>
            <p>
                Guests may use a guest account only through an authorized
                invitation. Guest access may expire, and it ends when an
                administrator removes it or invalidates the invitation or guest
                group.
            </p>
            <h3>Account security</h3>
            <p>
                Keep your password, passkeys, backup codes, and devices secure.
                Do not share an individual account with another person. If you
                believe an account has been compromised, tell your administrator
                or email <a
                    class="text-link"
                    href="mailto:support@origamisystems.org"
                    >support@origamisystems.org</a
                > right away.
            </p>
            <h2 id="organization-and-administrator-responsibilities">
                Organization and administrator responsibilities
            </h2>
            <p>Organizations and their administrators are responsible for:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Providing accurate account and organization information</li>
                <li>Assigning appropriate roles and permissions</li>
                <li>Removing access when a person leaves the Organization</li>
                <li>
                    Keeping single sign-on and directory provisioning settings
                    accurate, if they use them
                </li>
                <li>
                    Giving lawful instructions about organization-controlled
                    data
                </li>
                <li>Using invitations and guest groups responsibly</li>
                <li>
                    Responding to member, parent, and guardian requests about
                    records the Organization controls
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Administrators may create, view, update, archive, or remove
                accounts and organization information according to their
                permissions.
            </p>
            <h2 id="sign-up-forms">Sign-up forms</h2>
            <p>If you create a sign-up form, you are responsible for:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>What the form asks for and how you use the answers</li>
                <li>
                    Following the laws that apply to the information you
                    collect, including laws about children's information
                </li>
                <li>
                    Choosing the right visibility. On a standard form, anyone
                    who can open the form can see the names of the people signed
                    up. Turn on anonymous mode if participants should not see
                    each other.
                </li>
                <li>Keeping access codes private when you use them</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                If you register for a form, the form's creator and organizers
                will see your registration. Guests who register without an
                account receive a private cancellation link. Anyone with that
                link can cancel the registration, so keep it private.
            </p>
            <h2 id="acceptable-use">Acceptable use</h2>
            <p>You may not:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Break the law or violate another person's rights</li>
                <li>Harass, threaten, impersonate, or harm another person</li>
                <li>
                    Submit unlawful, deceptive, infringing, or malicious content
                </li>
                <li>
                    Collect information through a sign-up form that you have no
                    lawful reason to collect, or use forms for spam or phishing
                </li>
                <li>
                    Try to access another Organization, another person's
                    account, or data you are not permitted to see
                </li>
                <li>
                    Bypass roles, restrictions, rate limits, or security
                    controls
                </li>
                <li>
                    Share individual credentials or misuse invitations or
                    cancellation links
                </li>
                <li>Introduce malware or interfere with the Services</li>
                <li>
                    Scrape or automate access, except through a method we
                    authorize
                </li>
                <li>
                    Reverse engineer the Services, except where the law
                    expressly allows it
                </li>
                <li>Perform security testing without our written permission</li>
                <li>
                    Use the Services to build or improve a competing product
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                We may investigate suspected misuse and restrict access when
                reasonably necessary to protect users, Organizations, or the
                Services.
            </p>
            <p>
                If you find a security vulnerability, report it to <a
                    class="text-link"
                    href="mailto:support@origamisystems.org"
                    >support@origamisystems.org</a
                > and give us a reasonable time to fix it before sharing it publicly.
            </p>
            <h2 id="your-content">Your content</h2>
            <p>
                You or your Organization keep ownership of the content you
                submit to the Services.
            </p>
            <p>
                You give Origami Systems a limited, nonexclusive license to
                host, copy, process, transmit, and display that content only to
                operate, secure, support, and improve the Services and to meet
                our legal obligations. This license ends when the content is
                deleted from our active systems, except for copies in backups
                until they expire and information the law requires us to keep.
            </p>
            <p>
                You confirm that you have permission to submit the content and
                to let us process it under these terms. Organizations may
                moderate or remove content in their accounts. We may remove
                content that violates these terms.
            </p>
            <h2 id="our-property">Our property</h2>
            <p>
                Origami Systems and its licensors own the Services, including
                the software, design, documentation, and trademarks. We give you
                a limited, revocable, nontransferable right to use the Services
                under these terms. These terms do not transfer ownership of the
                Services to you.
            </p>
            <p>
                If you send us feedback, we may use it without restriction or
                payment. This does not give us ownership of your personal
                information or your content.
            </p>
            <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
            <p>
                Our Privacy Policy at <a class="text-link" href="/privacy"
                    >https://origamisystems.org/privacy</a
                > explains how we handle personal information. An Organization may
                also have its own privacy notices and legal duties for the information
                it controls.
            </p>
            <p>
                If an Organization has a separate service agreement or data
                processing agreement with Origami Systems, that agreement
                controls where it conflicts with these terms.
            </p>
            <h2 id="third-party-services">Third-party services</h2>
            <p>
                The Services rely on third-party providers for hosting, sign-in,
                email, payments, notifications, and error monitoring. Some
                features connect to services you or your Organization choose,
                such as Google, Microsoft, or an Organization's identity
                provider. Those services have their own terms. We are not
                responsible for a third-party service outside our reasonable
                control, but this section does not remove responsibilities that
                the law or our agreements place on us.
            </p>
            <h2 id="fees-and-payment">Fees and payment</h2>
            <p>
                Some Services or features require a paid plan. If you or your
                Organization buy one:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    You agree to pay the fees and taxes shown at checkout or in
                    your order.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Stripe processes payments. You authorize us, through Stripe,
                    to charge your payment method for each billing period.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Subscriptions renew automatically at the end of each billing
                    period until canceled.
                </li>
                <li>
                    You can cancel at any time in your billing settings or by
                    emailing <a
                        class="text-link"
                        href="mailto:support@origamisystems.org"
                        >support@origamisystems.org</a
                    >. Cancellation takes effect at the end of the current
                    billing period, and you keep access until then.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Fees are not refundable, except where the law requires a
                    refund or we agree to one in writing.
                </li>
                <li>
                    If a payment fails, we will notify you. If it is not
                    resolved within 14 days, we may suspend paid features until
                    it is.
                </li>
                <li>
                    We will give at least 30 days' notice before a price
                    increase takes effect on your next renewal.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                A separate order form or agreement with an Organization controls
                where it conflicts with this section.
            </p>
            <h2 id="suspension-and-termination">Suspension and termination</h2>
            <p>
                You may stop using the Services at any time. An Organization may
                ask to close its account by emailing <a
                    class="text-link"
                    href="mailto:support@origamisystems.org"
                    >support@origamisystems.org</a
                >, subject to any separate agreement.
            </p>
            <p>
                We may suspend or end your access if you materially violate
                these terms, create a security or legal risk, fail to pay
                required fees, or use the Services in a way that could harm
                another person or the Services. When practical, we will notify
                you first and give you a chance to fix the problem.
            </p>
            <p>
                When an Organization closes, we will give it 30 days to export
                its data. After that, we may delete the data as described in our
                Privacy Policy and any agreement with the Organization.
            </p>
            <p>
                Sections that by their nature should continue after termination
                remain in effect, including ownership, payment obligations,
                disclaimers, limits on liability, indemnification, and dispute
                terms.
            </p>
            <h2 id="disclaimers">Disclaimers</h2>
            <p>
                We work to keep the Services available and secure, but outages,
                maintenance, and errors happen. Unless a separate agreement says
                otherwise, we provide the Services "as is" and "as available."
            </p>
            <p>
                To the extent the law allows, Origami Systems disclaims implied
                warranties, including merchantability, fitness for a particular
                purpose, and noninfringement. This does not affect warranties or
                rights that cannot legally be excluded.
            </p>
            <h2 id="limitation-of-liability">Limitation of liability</h2>
            <p>
                To the extent the law allows, neither party will be liable for
                indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive
                damages, or for lost profits, revenue, or business
                opportunities, arising from the Services.
            </p>
            <p>
                To the extent the law allows, Origami Systems' total liability
                for all claims arising from the Services will not exceed the
                greater of (a) the fees you paid us for the Services in the 12
                months before the claim arose, or (b) $100.
            </p>
            <p>
                These limits do not apply to liability that cannot legally be
                limited, or to exceptions stated in a separate agreement with an
                Organization.
            </p>
            <h2 id="indemnification">Indemnification</h2>
            <p>
                To the extent the law allows, an Organization will defend and
                indemnify Origami Systems against third-party claims arising
                from the Organization's unlawful content, its misuse of the
                Services, or its material violation of these terms. This does
                not apply to claims caused by Origami Systems' own misconduct or
                violation of law.
            </p>
            <h2 id="changes-to-these-terms">Changes to these terms</h2>
            <p>
                We may update these terms. When we do, we will update the date
                above and give reasonable notice of material changes through the
                Services or by email. If the law requires it, or if a change is
                material, we will ask you to accept the new terms before you
                keep using the Services.
            </p>
            <p>
                The terms in effect when a claim arose govern that claim unless
                the parties agree otherwise or the law requires a different
                result.
            </p>
            <h2 id="governing-law-and-disputes">Governing law and disputes</h2>
            <p>
                Texas law governs these terms, without regard to conflict-of-law
                rules.
            </p>
            <p>
                Before filing a claim, contact us at <a
                    class="text-link"
                    href="mailto:support@origamisystems.org"
                    >support@origamisystems.org</a
                > and describe the dispute. Both sides will try in good faith to resolve
                it informally for 30 days. Either side may then go to court.
            </p>
            <p>
                Any court proceeding must be brought in the state or federal
                courts located in Denton County, Texas, unless the law requires
                another location. Either party may bring an individual claim in
                small claims court if it qualifies.
            </p>
            <h2 id="general-terms">General terms</h2>
            <p>
                These terms, our Privacy Policy, and any separate agreement with
                an Organization are the entire agreement about the Services. If
                any provision is unenforceable, the rest stays in effect. A
                failure to enforce a provision is not a waiver. You may not
                assign these terms without our written consent. We may assign
                them as part of a merger, reorganization, or sale of the
                Services.
            </p>
            <p>
                Neither party is responsible for delays caused by events beyond
                its reasonable control, except for payment obligations.
            </p>
            <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
            <p>
                Origami Systems LLC<br /><a
                    class="text-link"
                    href="mailto:support@origamisystems.org"
                    >support@origamisystems.org</a>
            </p>
        </div>
    </article>
</MainLayout>

<style>
    .blog {
        width: 80vw;
    }
    .blog header {
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
        text-align: left;
    }
    .blog header .description {
        color: var(--subtext-0);
    }
    .blog :global(.card) {
        width: 100%;
        max-width: none;
        margin-top: 1rem;
    }

    hr {
        width: 100%;
    }

    .summary-card {
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .summary,
    .content {
        text-align: left;
    }

    .summary h2 {
        margin-top: 0;
        font-size: 20px;
    }

    .summary-note {
        color: var(--subtext-0);
    }

    /* Match the blog post content components (src/components/content). */
    .content p,
    .content ul {
        margin: 0;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
    .content h2 {
        font-size: 26px;
        margin-top: 1rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }
    .content h3 {
        font-size: 24px;
        margin-top: 1rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
    }
    .content h4 {
        font-size: 20px;
        margin-top: 1rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
    }
    .content a {
        color: var(--accent);
        font-weight: 700;
        text-decoration: none;
    }
    .content a:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .content {
        counter-reset: section;
    }
    .content h2 {
        counter-increment: section;
        position: relative;
        padding-left: 2.5rem;
        scroll-margin-top: 80px;
    }
    .content h2::before {
        content: counter(section) ".";
        position: absolute;
        left: 0;
        font-weight: 600;
    }
</style>
